A vast, orderly garden maze viewed from above in the style of Piet Mondrian, with geometric pathways in primary colors (red, yellow, blue) and black grid lines dividing distinct sections. Some sections contain wild, organic flowering growth bursting beyond their boundaries, while others remain precisely trimmed and contained. A winding golden path connects the rigid outer sections to a vibrant, experimental center where multiple plant varieties intermingle freely. Small figures traverse different zones, some walking established routes, others exploring untamed areas. The composition balances strict rectangular divisions with natural chaos, suggesting harmony between structure and freedom, control and innovation.
